title: Convert TypeScript processEvent live entry into Rust
depends: AEP28-ENV-022
out_of_scope: hangar tools

note: ENV-022 removed sequential TypeScript deniers after aep-envelope Admit. TypeScript DynAEPBridge.processEvent still loads ActionLattice YAML, spawns aep-envelope, stamps the clock, ingests forecast coordinates, applies structure and mints IDs. Convert that live entry into Rust.

acceptance:
  - Live entry is Rust. aep-envelope admit is in-process (aep_envelope::admit). No spawnSync of aep-envelope on the live path.
  - ActionLattice YAML load is Rust.
  - Structural apply and ID minting are Rust.
  - TypeScript DynAEPBridge.processEvent is not the product live path.
  - CI fails if typescript dynaep processEvent still calls spawnSync, loadFromFile, processStateDelta or processDynAEPEvent as live product code.
  - Do not port TemporalValidator, UnifiedRegoEvaluator, UnifiedScanner or CausalOrderingEngine sequential deniers back into the Rust live path. Walls stay in aep-envelope collect-all then Apply.
  - AEP-SDKs/rust dynaep DynAepBridge is not a free copy of the old TypeScript sequential pipeline. Grow aep-envelope plus Rust apply.